               believed to be due to three different processes: (1) the
               ionization; (2) the nuclear scattering; (3) the emission of
               radiation under the influence of the electric field of a
               nucleus. The first two processes have been treated in quantum
               mechanics by Bethe, M{\o}ller, and Bloch in a very satisfactory
               way. A provisional estimation of the order of magnitude to be
               expected in the third process has been given by Heitler. The
               result obtained was that the cross-section ϕ for the energy loss
